  "body": "## Result and exact boundary\n\n347 genuine E8 frames on the fixed P107 live set have all 28 two-point\nframe-intersection graphs connected, but their coordinate-2 diagonal-incidence\nmatrix has rational rank 43 instead of the required 44. An explicit +/-1\nvector supplies an eighth independent kernel direction. This refutes\n**(G) implies (D) for selected frame subfamilies**, not for the family of all\nlive frames.\n\nThe complete 877-frame family satisfies all eight required ranks. Adding one\nexplicit omitted frame, whose extra-vector sum is 2, already repairs all eight\nranks. No nongauge decoder, supplier, copied-information floor, physical\nadoption, new kappa or selected-frontier change is claimed. In particular this\ndoes not refute the predecessor theorem, which assumes (D) independently.\n\n## Task card and sources\n\n- Assigned track: complex-mechanisms; OS nonce\n  `0d6468a107c6f96e18bdef01e3e8f622`; original card\n  `complex-rank-shape-decoder`, scope key `02b31ebd160542c86299`.\n- **Changed scope** to the connectivity-versus-rank handoff:\n  https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/discussions/1166#discussioncomment-18914508.\n  This is prerequisite-verification side work, not satisfaction of the card's\n  physical rank-shape acceptance gate. No proposed supplier means no replacement\n  moment or a<D/E invoice; selected baseline bindings and the card's ceiling\n  positive control were replayed.\n- Base: `858771bcca3b8dd5d4ef4aa682a13cc9b7e23920`.\n- Concrete object: FRAME0=(0,1,6,11,20,29,106,119),\n  X=(32,45,73,78,88), F=(2,5,8,9,30,41,108,117); coordinate 2;\n  select all live frames annihilating the recorded signed vector.\n- Criterion/fixture: https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/1560\n  at `eb9f6f15f15704949cbd25ca8fbf58063084dd8e`.\n- Open implication question: https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/1616\n  at `7b3e4624e31647fc2a8b777a181823739b12b36e`.\n- Entry and immediate refined-object overlap checks were run before computation.\n  Final refresh at 2026-10-14T05:10Z covered 593 open PRs and 292 discussions,\n  complete pagination, plus local notes and ledger. Relevant heads were unchanged.\n  No competing selected-subfamily investigation was found; unsearched diffs and\n  closed work outside local notes remain coverage limitations.\n- Claim: https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/discussions/1166#discussioncomment-18915387.\n\n## Files and verification\n\nOnly `research/e8-connectivity-incidence-boundary/` is added:\n`README.md`, `TASK.json`, `SOURCES.json`, `VERIFY.json`, `CERTIFICATE.json`,\n`verify.py`, `test_verify.py`. Frozen inputs and selected record are unchanged.\n\n```sh\npython3.12 -B scripts/research_package.py --package research/e8-connectivity-incidence-boundary --check-only\npython3.12 -B scripts/research_package.py --package research/e8-connectivity-incidence-boundary\n```\n\nObserved locally on Windows, Python 3.12: metadata/pins PASS; registered replay\nPASS; 2 unittest groups PASS, including five semantic/receipt rejection cases.\nVerifier output:\n\n```text\nPASS_E8_CONNECTIVITY_INCIDENCE_BOUNDARY live=877 selected=347 graphs=28 rank=43 required=44 canonical_kernel=7 extra_kernel=1 full_family_control=PASS one_frame_repair=PASS\n```\n\nInteger kernel identities supply exact upper rank bounds, modular nonzero minors\nsupply lower bounds, and the bounds meet. No floating point or predecessor\nchecker imports. A separate read-only AI review independently regenerated the\ngeometry/graphs and used Fraction elimination to reproduce selected/full ranks\n43/44, canonical/augmented kernel ranks 7/8 and repaired rank 44. Its two minor\ntest-feedback items were addressed and the registered replay rerun.\n\n## Remaining obligations and credit\n\nThe **all-live-frame-family** implication remains open and is the next question\nin the README/TASK. No downstream rigidity, cost-floor or full multiplication\nproof obligations are discharged. No full selected cold replay, independent\nhuman review or hosted-CI success is claimed.\n\nCredit Andrey Mas / an664 for the criterion and fixture, Josie Elliston for the\nhandoff and modular-rank methodology, and Brett Halligan / burntout76 /\nNinefold (https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/1212),\nDreamingOfClouds (https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/717),\nthemilkman216 (https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/968)\nfor the retained geometry/decoder lineage.\n\nPrepared by **Aaron Wang / navinor, with help from chatgpt**. Substantial AI\nassistance includes research, implementation, writing and read-only review.\nApache-2.0.\n\nWorkflow feedback: the concrete-term recheck found the precise open handoff;\nthe annihilator-selected first vector falsified the broader implication without\na larger search. The supplied Python-3.12 path lacked a backslash: the working\npath here is `C:\\Users\\warha\\.local\\bin\\python3.12.exe`. PowerShell 5's default\nredirection writes UTF-16; avoid it for JSON intended for UTF-8 tools. No packages\nwere installed.\n",
